bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_u8_array_into_i64_array_param_reads_zero_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (seed sha256 5347b0437924bb29, release/1.0.0 25308aa2aed, aarch64): fn at64(data: [i64], i: i64) -> i64: data[i]; fn relay(data) -> i64: at64(data, 1); with val b: [u8] = [1u8, 255u8, 128u8], relay(b) and at64(b, 1) print 255 in the interpreter and 0 under the JIT (no fallback, no diagnostic). Impact: hex_encoding.spl byte_at(data: [i64], ..) is called with [u8] by bytes_to_hex, so std.*.tls.utilities.bytes_to_hex([1u8, 255u8]) is 01ff interpreted and 0100 JIT. Either the checker must reject [u8] -> [i64] or the call must convert; byte_at should also take [u8]. Side note: a fn named pass gives semantic: value is not callable in the interpreter and a core dump under the JIT."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    seed_jit_u8_array_into_i64_array_param_reads_zero_2026-11-27, P2, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "Seed JIT: a [u8] array passed to a [i64] parameter is admitted and indexes as 0 (interpreter gives the byte); breaks TLS bytes_to_hex", src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/tls/_TlsUtilities/hex_encoding.spl, 342, NONE, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_u8_array_into_i64_array_param_reads_zero_2026-11-27, 3, "2026-11-27 opus-bugbatch trap parity (Fable follow-up on e0fab4aeaf6). The Rust trap printed 'error: <op>: ...' and aborted (status 134), while the C lane's rt_typed_words_byte_write_trap reaches runtime.c spl_panic, which prints 'PANIC: <msg>' and exits 1; the C selfcheck hid the gap with its own aborting spl_panic stub. Now the Rust trap prints the C line 'PANIC: typed word write: a [u8] array cannot be written through a word-typed array parameter ([i64]/[u64]/[u32])' and exits 1, the selfcheck stub mirrors runtime.c, and all three subprocess tests (runtime 7 ops, JIT 6 ops, C fork 6 ops) assert status 1 plus the message. Red: runtime test got status 134. Green: runtime lib 1577 passed, JIT file 4 passed, C selfcheck 90 checks. runtime_legacy_core.c spl_panic still prints a lowercase 'panic: ' prefix (core-C test kind); the C check matches the text after the prefix."
    seed_jit_u8_array_into_i64_array_param_reads_zero_2026-11-27, 2, "2026-11-27 opus-bugbatch review fixes (Fable FIX-FIRST on 482e816080e). (1) The Rust rt_typed_words_u32_set / u64_set had no byte-packed check and stored 8-byte slots into a [u8] (fn w(d: [u64], i, v): d[i] = v via an untyped relay wrote b0=72, the tagged 9). (2) The bound-proved loop (val n = d.len(); var i: u64 = 0; while i < n) over a [u32]/[u64] parameter reads through the hoisted data pointer (rt_typed_words_{u32,u64}_data_at / u64_raw_data_at): 8-byte loads past the bytes (origin JIT 8453889000000 vs 1255128). Fixed: MIR tags the hoisted word pointer bit 0 = byte-packed (the existing [u8] pointer uses the opposite tag), and the _data_at / _raw_data_at / _data_at_checked / _unchecked readers decode the byte on the Rust, C and Cranelift lanes. (3) Owner decision applied: a typed word write into a [u8] is a runtime error on both lanes (error message, abort), not a silent refusal; Rust set/push/push_known_at/push_known_data_at and the C slot helpers trap, the inlined [u32] set calls rt_typed_words_byte_write_trap on a cold branch, the inlined push sends a byte array to the trapping runtime push. Not guarded: rt_typed_words_*_store_known_data_at, reachable only through the append proof whose array local is created by a capacity new-array expression in the same function, so it cannot hold a [u8]. (4) Perf correction: 482e816080e made a [u32] read loop 2.9x slower (1.87 s -> 5.42 s, 1e9 reads) through a separate never-taken flag branch; the flag test is now folded into the bounds branch. 4 alternated rounds, origin c6f98def228712ea vs ba4bbc21cd7be722, 1e9 reads each: i64 at 1.935 vs 1.952 s, u32 at 1.897 vs 1.598 s, hoisted u64 1.970 vs 1.800 s, hoisted u32 1.455 vs 1.402 s, RSS 41 MB both: no regression. Red->green: runtime test_typed_words_hoisted_readers_decode_byte_packed_arrays (read 125894401) and test_typed_words_writers_trap_on_byte_packed_arrays (u32_set child exited cleanly); C selfcheck block 3 FAIL line=133 -> PASS 90 checks; JIT jit_hoisted_loop_readers_decode_bytes_from_untyped_caller (1056736000000 -> 1255128) and jit_word_array_writers_trap_on_bytes_from_untyped_caller (u32_set child exited cleanly -> all six writes abort with the message)."
    seed_jit_u8_array_into_i64_array_param_reads_zero_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-27 opus-bugbatch fix (reads widened correctly; static rejection deferred). Root: a byte-packed [u8] reaching a [i64]/[u64]/[u32] parameter (typed call or untyped relay) was read and written as 8-byte slots. Fixed: rt_typed_words_{i64,u64,u32}_at decode the byte in the Rust runtime and the C runtime (C word writers also refuse BYTES arrays, as the Rust ones already did); the Cranelift inliners for those readers branch byte-packed arrays to a 1-byte load; the inlined [u32] set and [u32]/[u64] push no longer store 8 bytes into a byte buffer (set refuses, push takes the refusing runtime call). Origin seed c6f98def228712ea JIT was silently wrong for in-tree crypto: sha256_bytes/hmac_sha256_bytes over [u8] gave a2d39892.../a29090.. vs the interpreter 8e3b08dc.../80d0ac12..., bytes_to_hex([u8]) gave empty text; d[1] = 77u32 on a [u8] through [u32] overwrote bytes 8..15 and an in-capacity [u64] push grew len past the buffer. Fixed seed 1f9fff26627b71df: all agree with the interpreter on JIT. Red->green: runtime test_typed_words_readers_decode_byte_packed_arrays (index 0 read 190473335537409), rt_array_hardening_selfcheck block 3 (FAIL line=100 -> PASS 81 checks), compiler/tests/seed_jit_u8_into_word_array_reader.rs readers (1000000 -> 1255128) and writers (1008 -> 16). Perf: 500M [i64] reads 1.012 s origin vs 0.932 s fixed, RSS 40 MB both. Remaining divergence, not fixed: JIT refuses word writes into a [u8] (silently, element unchanged) while the interpreter applies them; a word array into a [u8] param truncates out-of-range values on JIT (300->44) like scalar i64->u8, interpreter keeps 300. Owner decision: an E1003 rejection of [u8] into a wider-element param (patch kept at /home/yoon/dev/simple-handover/u8_into_word_array_e1003_rule_20261127.patch) breaks seed compile of in-tree callers: crypto sha256_bytes/hmac_sha256_bytes/hmac_sha384_bytes/bytes_to_hex take [i64] and tls13 hkdf, tls13_key_update, csrf_integration, audit_chain, rsa_pss, signed_build_* and dashboards pass [u8] (9 of 2503 sampled src files; 3 of them otherwise compile). Migrating those callees to [u8] precedes the rejection. Hoisted-loop variants (_unchecked, _data_at, store_known_data_at) were not reached by the probed shapes and are not guarded."

